Z||000000||johnmac||11-03-2000||05:29 AM||||Has anyone tried to put a cushion over the center console for a 3rd person. <P>If I add seatbelts and a cushion, I can legally bring along my 5 year old son.<P>I saw this on a Italian mid engine dream car some years ago.<P>Any ideals?<P>John<BR>John||||reg||1
Z||000001||Haze_Performance||11-03-2000||06:08 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by johnmac:<BR><B>Has anyone tried to put a cushion over the center console for a 3rd person. <P>If I add seatbelts and a cushion, I can legally bring along my 5 year old son.<P>I saw this on a Italian mid engine dream car some years ago.<P>Any ideals?<P>John<BR>John</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>All I have to say is "  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"> "<P><BR>P.S. Theres NO way.. The gas tank & computer are there. It would be VERY unsafe.<P><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/goodlogo1_1.gif"> ||||reg||5
Z||000002||HAGS||11-03-2000||06:18 AM||||I was thinking the same...I wouldnt want to be sitting on the gas tank, and if I were going to put a seat in I would chop up the console which would cause some stuff to move around...stuff that doesnt want to move.  I recommend putting him on the roof or the luggage rack  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000003||johnmac||11-03-2000||07:30 AM||||Yea, sometimes I like to put my son in a trailer behind me!!!<P>Seriously, If a 3 inch cushion was placed ontop the glovebox (ECM) and the console <BR>(gas tank)and only a 40# weight was distributed over same - - why not?<P>The ECM has side venting, no problem. And if the gas tank goes on fire - we is all inside the car in trouble. <P>Am I still Crazy!?<P>John MacHaffie||||reg||1
