Z||000005||stimpy||11-03-2000||08:27 AM||||I think the "Italian supercar" that you are speaking of was the Talbot-Matra Murena, actually a French car.  Pretty cool looking car that had a lot in common with the Fiero.  It was <B>considerably</B> wider however. I would think that that kid would outgrow that spot quickly. I wish there was some type of kit that turned the Fiero into a 2+2, kinda like the Ferarri 308 GT4.  I'd love to have about a foot of room between the seatback and the firewall.<P>More details on the Murena-&gt; <A HREF="http://www.matrasport.dk/Cars/Murena/murena-index.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.matrasport.dk/Cars/Murena/murena-index.html</A>  <BR>------------------<BR>Loud Pipes Save Lives!        <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/stimpy_sig.gif">   <P><p>[This message has been edited by stimpy (edited 11-03-2000).]||||reg||1
