Z||000015||MikeE||11-04-2000||04:43 PM||||Personally, who cares whether you can make it legal, it's the safety of your son that matters.  It doesn't sound very safe and no matter what you work out, you have no way of verifying the safety.  Consider this-how would you feel if you had an accident and you survived unscathed but your son was either severely injured or killed.  Would you blame yourself?  Probably, and that would haunt you for the rest of your life.  <P>Even with a kid's car seat securly fastened, his legs will be exposed to injury during a crash.  My 4 year old daughter still rides in a car seat and only in cars with a high crash rating and a low rollover rating.  Even then, she still rides in the middle back seat, and with the recent news report about the failure of GM seat backs she won't be riding in any GM cars that have bucket seats.  I say again, please consider how much your son means to you and rethink this.<P>[This message has been edited by MikeE (edited 11-04-2000).]<p>[This message has been edited by MikeE (edited 11-04-2000).]||||reg||1
